id: pm-linear-4yle
title: A test stub trims dashes with an alternation that is retried from every position
description: "CodeQL flagged js/polynomial-redos at test/atomic.test.ts line 31. The fakeNormalize stub trimmed dashes with a single alternation, caret dash plus or dash plus dollar, applied globally. In that alternation the trailing branch is retried from every position, so an input that folds to a long run of dashes costs quadratic time. It is a test stub rather than production code, so the exposure is bounded, but the fix is two separately anchored replacements which are linear and no less readable."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-31T12:06:57.931Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-31T12:06:59.750Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-31T12:06:59.737Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-31T12:06:59.737Z"
author: claude-orchestrator
resolution: The dash trim uses caret dash plus and dash plus dollar as two anchored replacements instead of one global alternation.
expected_result: Normalising an identifier is linear in the length of the input.
actual_result: "The trailing branch of the alternation was retried from every position, so an input folding to a long run of dashes cost quadratic time."
files[1]{path,scope}:
  test/atomic.test.ts,project
close_reason: "Replaced the single global alternation with two separately anchored replacements, which are linear in the input length."
body: ""
